                    <head>A Persianate South Asian album of ten folios, with five paintings and
                        drawings as well as five calligraphy specimens.</head>
                    <msContents>

                        <summary>This Persianate South Asian album of ten folios preserves five
                            paintings and drawings, as well as five Persian calligraphy specimens. A
                            majority of the folios bear the seal impression of <persName
                                role="fmo seal" ref="http://viaf.org/viaf/73846445"
                                key="person_73846445">Sir Elijah Impey (1732–1809)</persName>, who
                            served as Chief Justice in Calcutta.</summary>

                        <msItem xml:id="Indian_Drawings_05-item1">
                            <locus from="1a" to="1a">Folio 1a</locus>
                            <title>Pink cinquefoil against a gilt ground.</title>
                            <textLang mainLang="fa">Persian</textLang>
                            <decoNote>
                                <dimensions type="margin" unit="mm">
                                    <height>198</height>
                                    <width>110</width>
                                </dimensions>
                                <dimensions type="illustration" unit="mm">
                                    <height>177</height>
                                    <width>83</width>
                                </dimensions>
                            </decoNote>
                            <note>A French inscription appears abraded at right. This folio appears
                                constructed differently from the others in the album and appears
                                likely appended to the balance of the album overall.</note>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="Indian_Drawings_05-item2">
                            <locus from="1b" to="1b">Folio 1b</locus>
                            <title>An elderly Akbar hawking with Jahāngīr</title>
